# Conventions

- **MAX 500 LINES PER FILE** (ESLint `max-lines`). Split a file before it
  reaches ~400 lines. Components are split into subcomponents first.
- No code comments unless explicitly asked.
- Named exports everywhere. Default exports only in `frontend/src/app/**/page.tsx`
  and Next.js special files (`layout.tsx`, `middleware.ts`).
- Every user-facing string goes through `t('key')`; the key must exist in BOTH
  `frontend/src/i18n/en.ts` and `frontend/src/i18n/ur.ts`.
- Urdu is RTL: use logical Tailwind properties (`ms-`, `me-`, `ps-`, `pe-`,
  `text-start`, `text-end`), never `ml-`/`mr-`/`left-`/`right-`.
- No secrets in code — env only (`.env.example` documents every variable).
- Customer photos and measurements are private: never return them from public
  endpoints, never log them.
- Validation with Zod lives in the router as middleware; controllers never
  re-parse input.
- Errors: throw `AppError` from `backend/src/utils/errors.ts`; never leak stack
  traces or raw DB errors to clients.
